  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 134 AM CDT Sun Sep 6 2026\n\nA backdoor cold front pushed into the area yesterday evening, which \nwill bring \"relief\" today and Monday, where heat indices will be in \nthe mid 80s to near 90 and highs in the 80s to low 90s. These cooler \ntemperatures will warm back up to low to upper 90s by Tuesday and\nWednesday as the upper ridging builds back eastward once again.\nThere is a 20-30% chance of heat indices greater than 100 degrees\nsouth of I-70 Wednesday afternoon, from the LREF.\n\nA weak cold front will move through on Wednesday as the ridge gets \nbroken down by an upper low, potentially stalling out across IL. It \nwill bring another two day break from the sweltering mid to upper 90 \ntemperatures, dropping temperatures into the low to mid 80s before \nbuilding back to near 90 for the weekend. \n\nThe next chance for any rain will come Thursday with the greatest \nPOPs (50-70%) mainly near and south of I-72. A strengthening LLJ \nwill reinvigorate thunderstorm development along the stalled \nboundary. As of now, the machine learning models are not showing a \nsevere threat with these storms. The PWATs look to be around 1.8-2.2 \ninches and WPC has a marginal risk for excessive rainfall for day 5 \n(Thursday).",
